<title>LATVIA: C.BANK UPDATES FULL LICENSE-HOLDER LIST.</title>
<headline>C.BANK UPDATES FULL LICENSE-HOLDER LIST.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Latvian central bank said on</p>
<p>Thursday that the number of banks allowed to accept deposits</p>
<p>from individuals has increased to 19 from 15 during the second</p>
<p>quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that Aizkraukles Bank, Latvian</p>
<p>Investment Bank, Vereinsbank Riga and VEF Bank have received</p>
<p>full licenses since March.</p>
<p>The central bank provided a list of the fully licensed</p>
<p>banks, ranking them by capital and reserves.</p>
<p>  Nb Bank	    Cap.&amp;reserves (June30 vs March31,'97)</p>
<p>				 (in thousands of lats)</p>
<p>  1  Unibanka	     29,282	  27,464</p>
<p>  2  Parekss Bank	 28,621	  24,156</p>
<p>  3  Rigas komercbanka  13,800	  13,003</p>
<p>  4  Rietumu Bank	 13,762	  11,400</p>
<p>  5  Baltic Transit Bnk  8,507	   8,008</p>
<p>  6  Aizkraukles Bank    7,972	   N/A</p>
<p>  7  Zemes Bank	    7,419	   7,145</p>
<p>  8  Saules Bank	   5,575	   5,435</p>
<p>  9  Hansabank-Latvija   5,456	   3,573</p>
<p>  10 Investment Bank     5,168	   N/A</p>
<p>  11 Mortgage&amp;land Bank  4,377	   2,942</p>
<p>  12 Savings Bank	  4,041	   3,782</p>
<p>  13 Vereinsbank Riga    3,662	   N/A</p>
<p>  14 Maras Bank	    3,600	   3,590</p>
<p>  15 Trasta Bank	   3,153	   2,842</p>
<p>  16 Kapital-banka	 3,143	   2,632</p>
<p>  17 VEF Bank		2,823	   N/A</p>
<p>  18 Multibanka	    2,422	   2,396</p>
<p>  19 Societe Generale*   N/A	     N/A</p>
<p>NOTE: Societe Generale Riga branch</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom +371 722 66 93</p>
